{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '460,490p;565,602p;775,798p' test/dao/host/gate_test.clj && sed -n '1149,1169p' docs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md && git show 05130e07 -- docs/design/host-boundary/closure-clj.edn test/dao/host/gate_test.clj && git diff --name-status fdeb9370..origin/master -- src | rg '(\"'^D|''^R|siteset|lower.cljc|cst.cljc)'\"'\"","aggregated_output":"      (doseq [f forms] (walk f #{})))\n    @acc))\n\n\n(defn effect-calls\n  \"[[kind line] ...] for the resolved effect calls in forms, read on\n   lanes (default all): each lane resolves its own arms, ns form, defs and\n   locals, and a source site any lane resolves to an effect counts once.\"\n  ([forms] (effect-calls lanes forms))\n  ([ls forms]\n   (->> (for [l ls, fs (scan-features l)] fs)\n        (distinct)\n        (mapcat #(lane-effect-calls % forms))\n        (distinct)\n        (mapv (fn [[k line _]] [k line])))))\n\n\n;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n;; List 1 and list 2\n;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n(defn lane-specific?\n  [file]\n  (not (str/ends-with? file \".cljc\")))\n\n\n(def list-1-categories\n  \"The §8.1 rows (r9): what the row means, the slices that may clear its\n   files from list 1 (\\\"H2\\\" \\\"H3\\\" \\\"H4\\\": removed by that slice; :stays:\n   retained by design; :pending: H2 migrates the file but a JVM arm\n   survives until the owner decides OQ11, §13), and the §3.1 closure\n       (for [[f {:keys [category clears]}] list-1\n             problem (cond\n                       (not (contains? list-1-categories category))\n                       [[:unknown-category f category]]\n                       (not (contains? (get-in list-1-categories [category :clears]) clears))\n                       [[:slice-not-allowed f [category clears]]]\n                       :else [])]\n         problem)\n       (for [[f {:keys [category]}] list-1\n             :when (contains? list-1-categories category)\n             :let [ex (exceptions f)\n                   allowed (cond-> (:classes (list-1-categories category))\n                             (and ex (= (:category ex) category)) (conj (:class ex)))\n                   on-lanes (keep (fn [[l m]] (when (contains? m f) [l (get m f)])) lane-classes)]\n             problem (if (empty? on-lanes)\n                       [[:in-no-lane f nil]]\n                       (for [[l cs] (sort-by first on-lanes)\n                             :let [kind (cond (empty? cs) :empty-classes\n                                              (= #{:none} (set cs)) :class-none\n                                              (not-any? allowed cs) :class-not-in-category\n                                              :else nil)]\n                             :when kind]\n                         [kind f [l category (set cs)]]))]\n         problem)\n       (for [[f {:keys [category]}] exceptions\n             :when (not= category (get-in list-1 [f :category]))]\n         [:exception-category f [category (get-in list-1 [f :category])]])))))\n\n\n(defn committed-lane-classes\n  []\n  (into {} (map (fn [l] [l (into {} (map (juxt :file :classes) (:files (committed-closure l))))])\n                lanes)))\n\n\n(def profile-additions\n  \"§8.1's planned additions that have landed: the dao.host profile files,\n   permitted host arms by design (list 1, :profile). Nothing in the\n(defn scan\n  \"{file {:arms [line ...] :effects {kind [line ...]}}} for sources\n   {file text}, or {file {:error msg}} for a file that cannot be read.\"\n  [sources]\n  (into (sorted-map)\n        (map (fn [[file text]]\n               [file (try\n                       (let [forms (cond\n                                     (string? text) (read-forms text)\n                                     (:read-error text) (throw (ex-info (str \"cannot read file: \" (:read-error text))\n                                                                        {:file file}))\n                                     :else (throw (ex-info \"cannot read file\" {:file file})))]\n                         {:arms (if (lane-specific? file)\n                                  [:whole-file]\n                                  (non-exempt-arms forms))\n                          :effects (reduce (fn [m [k line]] (update m k (fnil conj []) line))\n                                           {}\n                                           (effect-calls (file-lanes file) forms))})\n                       (catch Exception e {:error (or (ex-message e) (str e))}))]))\n        sources))\n\n\n(defn gate\n  \"The gate over sources {file text}: {:verdict :pass|:fail|:scan-failure\nlane closures). What this table does **not** do: it does not add\n`:runtime-prereq` to the deferred row's classes, nor any deferred or codec\nclass to the seams row (an unrestricted \"any class for a lane-specific\nfile\" exemption is refused; the Dart Jing writer stays excluded from seams\nand on its H4 deletion path). The deferred design (§9) and the codec track\n(§8.3) each still own the files their class names, regardless of the\nlist-1 row that permits the arm.\n\nThe §8.1 runtime-prerequisites row also admits an invocation-local\nvalidation identity cache (eval-bridge amendment, astra ruling 2026-11-13):\n`src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc`'s `machine-data?` keeps a per-invocation visited map\nso shared closure graphs validate once per validation call. The cache's\nlifetime is one validation invocation; it preserves payload, metadata and\nexact-integer carrier validation; a cached success means validation\ncompleted; identity bookkeeping affects traversal cost only. The file's\nclosure class `:runtime-prereq` records this bounded runtime permission.\nThe tool lives at `src/dev/host_boundary/closure.clj` (H0's justified\ndeviation: the repo keeps dev tools under `src/dev/`), and the design's\nearlier `dev/host_boundary/` path is read as that.\n\n### 8.2 The host-library gate (H2, H3): executable references within the closure\ncommit 05130e07acc745fdc3b2da6fc4e0751f7e0afb42\nAuthor: Sonny To <son.c.to@gmail.com>\nDate:   Sun Nov 15 13:55:21 2026 +0700\n\n    fix(host-boundary): the §8.1 arms amendment per astra's ruling — yin/vm.cljc gains :runtime-prereq (eval-bridge invocation-local validation cache); cst.cljc closure-exempt via :deferred-stage; §8.1 prose documents the bounded runtime-cache permission\n\ndiff --git a/docs/design/host-boundary/closure-clj.edn b/docs/design/host-boundary/closure-clj.edn\nindex e4515f35..6262063b 100644\n--- a/docs/design/host-boundary/closure-clj.edn\n+++ b/docs/design/host-boundary/closure-clj.edn\n@@ -436,7 +436,7 @@\n   {:file \"src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc\",\n    :ns yin.vm,\n    :shared true,\n-   :classes #{:consumer :profile-consumer}}\n+   :classes #{:consumer :profile-consumer :runtime-prereq}}\n   {:file \"src/cljc/yin/vm/ast_walker.cljc\",\n    :ns yin.vm.ast-walker,\n    :shared true,\ndiff --git a/test/dao/host/gate_test.clj b/test/dao/host/gate_test.clj\nindex 7f65bce6..1dbded3f 100644\n--- a/test/dao/host/gate_test.clj\n+++ b/test/dao/host/gate_test.clj\n@@ -525,6 +525,7 @@\n    cannot go stale silently). A new row here is a §8.1 amendment.\"\n   {\"src/cljc/dao/space/transactor.cljc\"\n    {:category :deferred-scope :class :runtime-prereq\n+\n     :reason \"§8.1 deferred row (locking); §3.1 table C\"}\n    \"src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/authority.cljc\"\n    {:category :deferred-scope :class :runtime-prereq\n@@ -666,6 +667,7 @@\n    \"src/cljc/dao/data/btree.cljc\" (entry :runtime-prereq :stays \"atomic flag, weak/soft references\")\n    \"src/cljc/dao/data/btree/storage.cljc\" (entry :runtime-prereq :stays \"promise facade, deferred §9.1\")\n    \"src/cljc/dao/pretty.cljc\" (entry :runtime-prereq :stays \"display only\")\n+   \"src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc\" (entry :runtime-prereq :stays \"Invocation-local identity cache for machine-data? validation; eval-bridge amendment (astra s81-arms ruling)\")\n    ;; Codec-track files\n    \"src/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc\" (entry :codec-track :stays)\n    \"src/cljc/dao/stream/transit.cljc\" (entry :codec-track :stays)\nM\tsrc/cljc/yang/core/lower.cljc\nA\tsrc/cljc/yang/core/siteset_publication.cljc\nA\tsrc/cljc/yang/core/siteset_store.cljc\nR053\tsrc/clj/yang/io.clj\tsrc/cljc/yang/io.cljc\nM\tsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/cst.cljc\nM\tsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc\nD\tsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/quoted.cljc\nM\tsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/siteset.cljc\nM\tsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc\nM\tsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc\nM\tsrc/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/lower.cljc\nD\tsrc/cljs/yang/io.cljs\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
