{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_27","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/cst.cljc; sed -n '715,760p;1035,1057p;1290,1312p' docs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md; sed -n '1,87p' test/dao/host/gate_test.clj; ls -ld .claude/worktrees/dao-host-gate-fix; git config --get core.hooksPath; git status --porcelain .claude/worktrees/dao-host-gate-fix\"","aggregated_output":"(ns yang.php.antlr.cst\n  \"The PHP parser worker (docs/design/yang.php.md section 6): the\n   grammars-v4 php grammar profile over the generic `yang.antlr.cst` worker.\n   The generated recognizers come from `bb gen:antlr` (antlr/php/manifest.edn);\n   the JVM and Node use the same grammar and export profile. The entry rule is `htmlDocument`.\n\n   The grammar's non-standard generics (`typeParameterListInBrackets`, the\n   `<: ... :>` brackets) are not PHP: a parse that uses them is refused as\n   `{:yang.php/not-php :generics}` rather than exported.\"\n  (:require\n    [yang.antlr.cst :as cst]\n    [dao.host.text :as text]\n    #?@(:cljs [[\"/yang/antlr/gen/php/PhpLexer.js\" :default PhpLexer]\n               [\"/yang/antlr/gen/php/PhpParser.js\" :default PhpParser]]))\n  #?(:clj (:import (yang.php.antlr.gen PhpLexer PhpParser))))\n\n\n(def grammar-id\n  \"grammars-v4 php at its pinned revision, generated by ANTLR 4.13.2.\"\n  \"grammars-v4/php@85e2dd1779ce556111ef98ead5d62a9858e95599 antlr-4.13.2\")\n\n\n(def profile\n  {:grammar-id grammar-id,\n   :make-lexer (fn [cs] (PhpLexer. cs)),\n   :make-parser (fn [ts] (PhpParser. ts)),\n   :start #?(:clj (fn [^PhpParser p] (.htmlDocument p))\n             :cljs (fn [^js p] (.htmlDocument p)))})\n\n\n(defn make-worker\n  []\n  (cst/make-worker profile))\n\n\n(defn make-eval-worker\n  \"A worker whose lexer starts in PHP mode with default mode underneath.\"\n  []\n  (cst/make-worker\n    (assoc profile :make-lexer\n           (fn [cs]\n             (let [lexer (PhpLexer. cs)]\n               #?(:clj (.pushMode lexer PhpLexer/PHP)\n                  :cljs (.pushMode lexer (.-PHP PhpLexer)))\n               lexer)))))\n\n\n(defn- generics?\n  [pk]\n  (boolean (some #(= \"typeParameterListInBrackets\" (:rule %))\n                 (:yang.cst/nodes pk))))\n\n\n(defn- line-starts\n  \"The UTF-8 byte offsets at which each source line begins (the line side\n   table, section 17: derived at the parse boundary, where the source is\n   known, so no later stage needs the text).\"\n  [source]\n  (let [bs (text/utf8-encode source)]\n    (into [0] (keep-indexed (fn [i b] (when (= b 10) (inc i)))) bs)))\n\n\n(defn parse-source\n  \"Parse one complete PHP source string as unit `unit`: the CST packet, or\n   `{:yang.php/not-php :generics}` when the parse uses the grammar's generics\n   extension.\"\n  ([source] (parse-source (make-worker) [:unit 0] source))\n  ([worker unit source]\n   (let [pk (cst/parse-unit worker unit source)]\n     (if (generics? pk)\n       {:yang.php/not-php :generics}\n       (assoc pk :yang.php/line-starts (line-starts source))))))\n    behaviour changes); H2 rewires `yin.vm.integer` to delegate and\n    deletes its copy, and switches `yang/php.cljc:95-97` to\n    `decimal-text->float`. `Double/parseDouble`, `js/parseFloat` and Dart\n    `double.parse` are nearest-even on this grammar (R), so the PHP float\n    path is not a behaviour change; the integer path at `:98-100` is (§10).\n- `dao.host.text/code-points` is callable from `dao.host` with no `yin`\n  require (V): the private `data.cljc:143-159` is written over\n  `unit-count` and `code-unit` only, which are Table A text entries; its\n  surrogate cases exist in `data_test.cljc` (`non-bmp-code-points-test`).\n\n**Table C: runtime prerequisites (documented and verified by existing\nsuites; not profile entries; not a boundary).**\n\n+----------------------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+---------+\n| Prerequisite                     | Where, and the law a port must meet (V)                                                        | Slice   |\n+==================================+================================================================================================+=========+\n| `deftype` with per-host          | `values.cljc:39-119`: `Closure`/`Continuation` equal iff owner and payload equal; hash of      | H1 docs |\n| equality, hashing and printing   | `[:tag owner payload]`; print the marker text. `cbor.cljc:342-460`: `Float64` equal by bits    |         |\n|                                  | with NaN equal to NaN (`:365-367`); `Rational`, `Decimal` equal by fields; hashes at           |         |\n|                                  | `:372-444`.                                                                                    |         |\n+----------------------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+---------+\n| Atomic flag                      | `btree.cljc:87-119`: transient ownership token readable across threads.                        | none    |\n+----------------------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+---------+\n| Weak and soft references         | `btree.cljc:182-245`; default `:soft` on the JVM, `:strong` on JS and Dart (`:39-44`). A host  | none    |\n|                                  | without them declares `:strong`; correctness is unchanged, retention differs.                  |         |\n+----------------------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+---------+\n| `locking`, atoms, volatiles      | Five `locking` sites (§3.1); single-owner discipline elsewhere.                                | none    |\n+----------------------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+---------+\n| Host promise type                | `btree/storage.cljc:218-227`: deferred (§9.1).                                                 | defer   |\n+----------------------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+---------+\n| Dialect syntax                   | §3.3.                                                                                          | H0      |\n+----------------------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+---------+\n\nLayering: `dao.host.*` requires nothing in the repo; `dao` never requires\n`yin`. Consumers after H2: `dao.jing`, `dao.jing.cbor`, `yin.vm.integer`,\n`yin.vm.data`, `yin.vm.values`, `yin.vm.engine`, `yin.vm`, `yin.vm.debruijn`,\n`yin.vm.debruijn-code`, `dao.stream.chunks`, `dao.jing.dht`, `yin.vm.linker`,\n`yin.vm.linker.sign`, `dao.stream.datagram`, `dao.stream.base64`, and the\nthree Python integer tests.\n\n### 4.3 Oracle coverage matrix (table D)\n\nEntry to exact file and case. V = the case exists today and exercises the\nbehaviour through its present namespace; P = proposed, written in the slice\nnamed. After H1 every V case is additionally run against `dao.host.*`\ndirectly by `dao.host.conformance-test` (P), which requires the new\nthe deferred row. **Two vocabularies, kept distinct (R7-4)**: a **closure\nclass** (the `:classes` set on each file in the committed edn, generated\nfrom the `class-rows` data in `closure.clj:112`, V) answers \"what host\ncontact does this file have\" per §3.1; a **gate category** (the\n`list-1-categories` of `gate_test.clj:444`, V) answers \"why is this file\npermitted a non-exempt arm\" per §8.1. The mapping is many-to-one and the\ngate test asserts it. **What H0 must change**: edit the classification\n**data** (the `class-rows` of `closure.clj`, which the worktree already\nextends with `:profile-consumer` and `:dialect-arm`, and the gate's list 1\ncategories) so that no entry is `:h0-unlisted`, then regenerate the edn\noutputs; drop nothing (the six names H0 could not find were never on the\ngenerated list, and the rows above no longer name them). **What H0 must\nnot change**: the traversal algorithm and its resolution rule, the totals\n142/140/141 and 133 shared, the independent-traversal agreement, the two\nnegative tests' semantics, the scan-failure test and the corpus hash set;\nthe lanes need not be re-run beyond `dao.host.gate-test` and the tool's\n`--check`. **How H1 and H2 clear\nthe tag**: H1 adds no consumer, so the nine stay tagged `:migration-source`;\nH2 migrates them with the other consumers and removes **eight** of them\nfrom list 1 in the same commit, which the `list-1-equals-the-observed-arms`\ntest enforces. The ninth, `yin/vm.cljc`, is **exempt pending OQ11**: after\nH2 its one-arity `bytes->str` is portable, but the JVM-only two-arity\nencoding form (`vm.cljc:404-406`, V) keeps one reader arm until the owner\nuncertainty, and test post-rename failure explicitly; short reads, partial\nappends, acquisition outcomes (`held`/`refused`/`unsupported`), durability\noutcomes per the declared failure model; `own-pid`, `process-alive?`,\n`create-exclusive!`, `unlink!`, `canonical-path` for the claim-file lock.\n\n### 9.3 The parser stage (reserved H7)\n\nIntent: the grammar profile plus host walk as one seam value; a\nremote-stage test. Required input: none beyond the stage's own host walk;\nr3's \"one `println`\" at `yang/python/antlr/repl.cljc:71` was inside a\nquoted yin program (the VM's primitive, not a host call, V) and is\nwithdrawn.\n\n### 9.4 Stream-implementation conformance and the wasm import gate (reserved H8)\n\nIntent: the contract's outcome tables through a scripted seam against every\nimplementation; a gate asserting a wasm binary's import list against the\nseven names. Required input: which implementations declare which outcome\nsubset (`dao.stream.md`, Surfaces).\n\n## 10. Cost and what would reverse this (H0-H4)\n\nCost (P, from §1 and §8.3, revised r7 for H0's finding): **24 existing\n(ns dao.host.gate-test\n  \"The H0 freeze gate of docs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md (§8 H0,\n   §8.1, §3.2, §3.3), over the adopted closure committed by\n   src/dev/host_boundary/closure.clj under docs/design/host-boundary/.\n\n   The gate reads every closure file with tools.reader (:read-cond\n   :preserve, so every lane's arms are seen; comments, strings and\n   docstrings never count) and fails when\n   - a file outside list 1 holds a non-exempt host arm (§3.3 exempts:\n     ns-form arms, catch-type arms, arms equal but for hints, protocol\n     blocks directly inside deftype/defrecord/reify/extend bodies,\n     print-method defmethods, exists? tests, (Object.)/(js-obj)\n     sentinels); a lane-specific file (.clj .cljs .cljd) is a host arm as\n     a whole;\n   - a file holds more resolved effect calls of a kind than list 2\n     permits (the §3.2 kinds, and calls of the §2.4 M entries).\n   Effect calls are resolved lexically: a symbol bound by let, fn, loop,\n   for, doseq, catch, letfn or a deftype method, defined in its file, or\n   excluded by :refer-clojure, is not the core function; quoted forms and\n   (comment ...) are data. Reading zero files, or failing to read one, is\n   a scan failure, distinct from a pass.\n\n   JVM lane only: the gate reads source text from disk; what it checks is\n   the same text on every lane.\n\n   Also here: the independent second traversal of the closure (a\n   reader-form walker that selects reader-conditional arms itself and\n   parses libspecs itself, sharing no code with tools.namespace), which\n   must agree with the committed closure files.\"\n  (:require\n    [clojure.edn :as edn]\n    [clojure.java.io :as io]\n    [clojure.set :as set]\n    [clojure.string :as str]\n    [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n    [clojure.tools.reader :as reader]\n    [clojure.tools.reader.reader-types :as rt])\n  (:import\n    (clojure.lang\n      ReaderConditional)))\n\n\n;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n;; Reading\n;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n(defn read-forms\n  \"Every top-level form of text, reader conditionals preserved.\"\n  [text]\n  (binding [reader/*read-eval* false\n            ;; ::alias/kw needs no real namespace: keywords never count\n            reader/*alias-map* (fn [sym] sym)\n            reader/*default-data-reader-fn* (fn [tag v] (tagged-literal tag v))]\n    (let [rdr (rt/indexing-push-back-reader text 1)]\n      (loop [acc []]\n        (let [form (reader/read {:read-cond :preserve :eof ::eof} rdr)]\n          (if (= ::eof form) acc (recur (conj acc form))))))))\n\n\n(defn rc?\n  [x]\n  (instance? ReaderConditional x))\n\n\n(defn rc-arms\n  \"[[feature form] ...] of a reader conditional.\"\n  [^ReaderConditional rc]\n  (map vec (partition 2 (.-form rc))))\n\n\n(defn splicing?\n  [^ReaderConditional rc]\n  (boolean (.-splicing rc)))\n\n\n(defn head\n  [x]\n  (when (and (seq? x) (symbol? (first x))) (first x)))\n\n\n(defn line-of\n  [x]\n  (:line (meta x)))\n\n\n;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n;; The independent closure traversal (traversal B)\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 58 sto  staff  1856 Nov 22 15:05 .claude/worktrees/dao-host-gate-fix\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
